troski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.11860531203093161,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":87.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.1285354170861619,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":89.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.029598453913394447,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":44.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.005152397156877653,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":43.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010198574170808517,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":83.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.108839996,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":72.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"HomeTrust Bancshares, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for HomeTrust Bank that provides a range of retail and commercial banking products and services in the United States. It's deposit products include savings, money market, noninterest-bearing, and interest-bearing checking accounts, as well as certificates of deposit for individuals, businesses, and nonprofit organizations. The company's loan portfolio comprises one-to-four-family real estate lending, multifamily, home equity lines of credit, construction and land development, indirect auto finance, and consumer lending; and commercial loans that include commercial real estate, construction and land development, and commercial and industrial loans. It also provides small business administration loans, equipment finance leases, and municipal leases, as well as cash management and online/mobile banking services. In addition, the company invests in debt securities issued by the United States government agencies and government-sponsored enterprises, municipal bonds, corporate bonds, commercial paper, and certificates of deposit insured by the federal deposit insurance corporation. Further it provides healthcare banking, designed to serve the distinct financial needs of healthcare practices and professionals; provides customized financial solutions and relationship-driven support for medical, dental, and veterinary practices throughout each stage of the business lifecycle, from acquisition and ownership transition to expansion and long-term operations. HomeTrust Bancshares, Inc. was founded in 1926 and is headquartered in Asheville, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. C. Hunter Westbrook | CEO, President & Vice Chairperson of the Board | Age 62 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 586 people. Revenue per employee of $364K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 10%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $77K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["HomeTrust Bancshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $743M market cap on $213M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $45M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.77\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3395698.96},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 55% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"HomeTrust Bancshares, Inc. (NYSE:HTB) Stock Rated \u201cModerate Buy\u201d by Sell-Side Brokerages","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/hometrust-bancshares-inc-nysehtb-stock-rated-moderate-buy-by-sell-side-brokerages.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793790923.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.832,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Comparing Plumas Bancorp (NASDAQ:PLBC) and HomeTrust Bancshares (NYSE:HTB)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/comparing-plumas-bancorp-nasdaqplbc-and-hometrust-bancshares-nysehtb.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793755724.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical Review: HomeTrust Bancshares (NYSE:HTB) versus First Bank (NASDAQ:FRBA)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/28/critical-review-hometrust-bancshares-nysehtb-versus-first-bank-nasdaqfrba.html","date":"2026-10-28","timestamp":1793219568.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.876,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (HTB) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/Trading_the_Move,_Not_th